ing for a longer period than one year, or for the sale, of any real property, or an interest therein, is void un- less the contract or some note or memorandum thereof, expressing the consideration, is in writing, subscribed by the party to be charged, or by his lawful agent thereunto authorized by writing. 3. A contract to devise real property or establish a trust of real property, or any interest therein or right with reference thereto, is void unless the contract or some note or memorandum thereof is in writing and subscribed by the party to be charged therewith, or by his lawfully authorized agent. 4. Nothing contained in this section abridges the powers of courts of equity to compel the specific performance of agreements in cases of part performance. REPRESENTATIVE STATUTES OF FRAUDS"